2297-- 最多 63 次请求，独立上限仍 $1.50、30 分钟；不自动重试、不调整旧预算。通过开发案例才谈后续验证，不直接启用默认管线或封存；失败报告，不自行改尺续开臂。
2298-
2299-- D162 result: the registered comparison failed end to end. All six sequences completed, 45 calls, estimated $0.6928525. First-step cost selection improved, but invalid ownership, wrong grouping, a period-check merge override and an inaccurate numerical summary remain. No default promotion. 227 Python tests passed. Evidence: `poc/reports/2026-10-25-source-first-01/results.md`.
2300-
2301-## D163 · 2026-10-25 · English for the maintained project
2302-
2303-- Alex: “let’s also use this chance to convert everything into english from chinese.” English becomes the language for maintained prompts, generated explanations, UI text and current documentation. Original source quotations and historical records retain their original language and identity.
2304-- The D162 experiment finishes under its original frozen requests. Language conversion is a separate change, not an unregistered experimental arm and not evidence that the extraction defects are fixed.
2305-- Inventory exact schema values and their readers before conversion. Preserve the ability to read existing records; no in-place rewriting of historical databases, frozen prompts, raw answers or prior decisions. New decisions and reports are written in English.
--
2356-- Fixed: the preflight's matching section now judges Jev records (it had skipped all 250 of the Jev ledger) and fails when every record of a ledger is skipped; the cost reports read the one price table (`model.PRICES`) and refuse an unpriced model; the benchmark stops when its evidence scorer fails; Jev succession eligibility has one rule (`jev_matching.can_succeed`); a test no longer reads the real credentials file, another no longer writes the real service archive; the newsroom category rule has one owner that its test exercises; the replay requires the ledger and archive it writes and defaults to `poc-v23` and the current item window; the compose file uses the adopted idea configuration `poc-v9`.
2357-- Left, with the reason: the dependency-cycle pass in `matching.check` (its refusal wording reaches stored retry requests, so merging it would change replayed requests); the two ladder validators (admission of a new ladder and reading of a stored one are different jobs); splitting `matching.check`, `writing._write` and `idea.read_idea` (behaviour-preserving refactors of the core without a measurement round); unused parameters and result fields (signature churn across many call sites); the corpus harvesters' shared fetch code; the test-only `search.fake_embed` in the search module; `scripts/review_english_run.py` counting equal model-written scopes as a breach (D155 makes them a lead, not identity). The reviewers' lead that the API's `poc-v9` default was stale was wrong: it is the adopted idea configuration (D135/D145).
2358-
2359:## D171 · 2026-10-25 · Review and free proofs for the day-batch acceleration proposal
2360-
2361-- Alex asked to review the extraction/Jev/per-day acceleration plan deeply and test it against the stored golds and result databases. Scope is review and isolated offline proofs; no product-contract change, runtime adoption or paid comparison follows automatically.
2362-- The [review](research/2026-10-25-day-batch-review/review.md) and its scripts reconstruct 960/960 extraction requests from the two saved v23 ledgers. Day-start context differs for 214/480 Jev-arm requests and 168/480 control requests; rechecking the same raw answers with day-start IDs loses 73/797 and 62/744 evidence items. Extraction depends on earlier theses as well as groups. The Jev arm has 86/320 final repeat/replace decisions targeting same-day evidence, and Jev membership alone cannot declare the 26 new groups.
2363-- At 32 workers, a three-wave schedule using recorded Jev call durations projects 8.6× on July 27 and 3.2× over 31 nonempty days, before reconciliation/rate-limit overhead. This replaces the unsupported general 10× claim, not the speed target. It is a schedule estimate, not fresh measured latency. Judging already uses six workers per dependency level.
2364-- Recommendation awaiting Alex's choice: concurrent request preparation with exact read validation before sequential commits, retaining D149/D159 semantics; re-run requests whose inputs changed. A more aggressive day-start extraction contract must be decided and tested separately. The review defines both boundaries, failure/recovery states, local-ID namespacing, evaluation limits and staged tests.
2365-- Verification: 128 product/corpus/diagnostic tests passed; two diagnostic mutants were caught; preflight judged 250 stored Jev records with no skipped records. Existing golds remain unchanged. No batching runtime or fresh model-quality pass is claimed.
2366-- A read-only review independently reproduced the 960 request message pairs and schemas, the stale-reference losses and the timing projection; no serious finding against the proposed contract. Runtime implementation and live measurement remain the next, separate steps.
2367-
2368:## D172 · 2026-10-25 · Build the isolated ordered-concurrency POC
2369-
2370-- Alex accepted the D171 recommendation: “yes be super careful about the logic ... do not fuck up the order ... flag it immediately”. Implement concurrent preparation with current-prefix validation and one ordered writer. Keep the default serial path and its tests unchanged. Group ownership and thesis/evidence semantics do not move.
2371-- Speculative calls may precede earlier commits in the experimental path; accepted handovers and writes may not. Stale prepared requests are recomputed; earlier failure cancels pending work and drains running calls without accepting later results. This scheduling distinction is explicit, not an accidental weakening of D159.
2372-- The [first implementation slice](research/2026-10-25-day-batch-review/implementation.md) covers offline coordinator, independent Jev calls and failure/restart verification on temporary storage. No paid call, new spending cap or default activation is authorized by this slice. The current per-item spend check is not safe reservation accounting for concurrent paid calls; resolve it before a live comparison.
2373-- Offline slice result: [ordered-concurrency POC](../poc/reports/2026-10-25-concurrency-poc/results.md). Shared request identity prevents conflicting concurrent answers under one archive ID. Bounded Jev submission cancels pending work on failure; the daily cost log includes discarded speculative work. Default replay remains serial. 143 tests pass; five intended mutants fail; 3,595 historical request hashes are unchanged. Final focused review finds no serious issue. Live accounting, fresh controls and speed measurement remain outstanding; no paid ingestion calls were made.

